# {{name}}

Perysee module `{{id}}`.

- `module.json`: identity, version, minimum Core version, dependencies and entitlement.
- `src/ModuleServiceProvider.php`: what the module adds to Perysee (see the options below).
- `routes.php`: the module's routes, served under `/modules/{{id}}`. Route names start with `{{id}}.`.
- `dist/module.js`: the compiled UI. It reaches Vue and Inertia through `Perysee.Vue` and `Perysee.Inertia`.

## Extending Perysee

A module adds to what exists instead of getting its own corner:

| In the provider | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `loadModuleRoutes($file)` | Pages and actions for signed-in users |
| `loadPublicRoutes($file)` | Routes without a session, under `/modules/{{id}}/public` |
| `addNavigation($zone, $label, $icon, $route)` | An entry in the `workspace` or `admin` navigation |
| `shareData($closure)` | Data for your screens, as `modules.data["{{id}}"]` |
| `brand($closure)` | Instance name, logo address and accent color |
| `listen($eventClass, $listener)` | React to a Core event such as `GoalConverted` or `ModuleQuarantined` (needs `"core": "0.4.0"` or later) |
| `notificationChannel($key, $channel)` | Declare a way to notify someone, such as a chat or a webhook (same requirement) |
| `reportSource($key, $source)` | Add figures to periodic reports (same requirement) |

| In `dist/module.js` | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `Perysee.registerSettings("{{id}}", component)` | The module's settings page, under Settings > Modules |
| `Perysee.registerSlot("site.report.after", component, { module: "{{id}}" })` | A block under a site report (also `dashboard.after`) |
| `Perysee.registerScreen("module:{{id}}", component)` | A full page |

Settings can be stored with `App\Modules\ModuleSettings` (`get`, `set`, `forget`, `all`).

Enable it with `php artisan perysee:modules enable {{id}}`, or from Settings > Modules.
